-"Yeah, it's just gnarly."

00:09:40.033 --> 00:09:41.501
-"It is gnarly.

00:09:41.501 --> 00:09:44.868
And at the end of the night,
do a little mezcalito."

00:09:44.868 --> 00:09:47.801
[ Laughter ]

00:09:47.801 --> 00:09:50.167
-I like that.
He's, like, a gnarly, cool dude.

00:09:50.167 --> 00:09:53.000
-Yeah, dude. Just turn
a negative into a positive.

00:09:53.000 --> 00:09:54.167
-That's so funny.

00:09:54.167 --> 00:09:55.868
I want to talk about
"Don't Worry Darling."

00:09:55.868 --> 00:09:57.067
Number one, by the way.

00:09:57.067 --> 00:09:59.000
And congratulations to you.
-Thank you.

00:09:59.000 --> 00:10:00.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:10:00.300 --> 00:10:01.701
-You're the star of the film.

00:10:01.701 --> 00:10:04.000
-I am the --
I am the star of that film.

00:10:04.000 --> 00:10:06.000
-You got applause
in the screening I saw.

00:10:06.000 --> 00:10:07.334
-Hey.
-Because you got a lot of fans

00:10:07.334 --> 00:10:09.300
here at "The Tonight Show."
We all like Nick Kroll.

00:10:09.300 --> 00:10:10.667
And we all clapped for you.

00:10:10.667 --> 00:10:14.834
No, but this film, I will say,
obviously, we all know,

00:10:14.834 --> 00:10:16.234
has a lot of drama behind it,

00:10:16.234 --> 00:10:19.734
people saying all
these stories about, you know --

00:10:19.734 --> 00:10:21.901
-Mm-hmm.
-And you told me this.

00:10:21.901 --> 00:10:23.200
You're the mastermind
behind all of it.

00:10:23.200 --> 00:10:24.634
-Yeah, so, the movie --

00:10:24.634 --> 00:10:27.467
So, if you haven't seen it yet,
it's, like, a thriller.

00:10:27.467 --> 00:10:29.467
And I think the less you know

00:10:29.467 --> 00:10:31.934
about the movie going in,
the better

00:10:31.934 --> 00:10:35.033
so that when you're watching it,
it's all new and surprising.

00:10:35.033 --> 00:10:40.801
So, I decided, "Let's create
a lot of buzz around the film."

00:10:40.801 --> 00:10:41.901
-Oh, it's genius.

00:10:41.901 --> 00:10:45.067
-"But not about
the film itself, right?"

00:10:45.067 --> 00:10:46.901
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:10:46.901 --> 00:10:50.767
-You are a genius, a mastermind.

00:10:50.767 --> 00:10:53.434
-You know, I'm the little --
I'm the puppeteer.

00:10:53.434 --> 00:10:55.701
And so I was like,
"Hey, Harry, you know what

00:10:55.701 --> 00:10:57.234
would be a great idea?

00:10:57.234 --> 00:11:00.634
When you walk into the premiere
in Venice, spit on Chris Pine."

00:11:00.634 --> 00:11:01.701
[ Laughter ]

00:11:01.701 --> 00:11:03.767
-Yeah.
-And he was like, "Got it."

00:11:03.767 --> 00:11:05.968
But then, he was like, "I don't
know if that's gonna work."

00:11:05.968 --> 00:11:07.567
So, then I was like,
"You know what?

00:11:07.567 --> 00:11:11.100
Maybe you should just,
you know, give me a kiss."

00:11:11.100 --> 00:11:12.934
And --
-Oww!

00:11:12.934 --> 00:11:15.701
-Get ready, Harry fans.
-And so --

00:11:15.701 --> 00:11:18.667
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:11:18.667 --> 00:11:21.634
And I -- And then I asked him
to spit in my mouth.

00:11:21.634 --> 00:11:22.968
[ Laughter ]
-He wouldn't do it.

00:11:22.968 --> 00:11:26.167
-He wouldn't do that.
The guy's got boundaries.

00:11:26.167 --> 00:11:30.200
And so, it ended up --
Anyway, but it ended up working.

00:11:30.200 --> 00:11:32.334
-What can we say
about the movie?

00:11:32.334 --> 00:11:34.300
'Cause I don't want
to give anything away.

00:11:34.300 --> 00:11:36.300
I could spoil it
in one sentence.

00:11:36.300 --> 00:11:38.133
-Yeah, I mean --
So the movie is like --

00:11:38.133 --> 00:11:39.634
-I'm not going to do that.
-I mean, you're welcome to.

00:11:39.634 --> 00:11:40.667
The movie is out.

00:11:40.667 --> 00:11:43.667
It's the number-one movie
in America.

00:11:43.667 --> 00:11:45.434
-You're gonna go for two --
let's go for two.

00:11:45.434 --> 00:11:47.667
Let's go for two weeks in a row.
-Two weeks, baby.

00:11:47.667 --> 00:11:50.367
-It's got good buzz.
-So the movie is like --

00:11:50.367 --> 00:11:52.801
It feels like
a utopian community,

00:11:52.801 --> 00:11:55.234
late '50s, early '60s.

00:11:55.234 --> 00:11:57.000
-Everything's perfect.
-Everything's kind of perfect,

00:11:57.000 --> 00:11:59.400
and they're working
on this project.

00:11:59.400 --> 00:12:03.601
And -- But things
aren't exactly as they seem.

00:12:03.601 --> 00:12:05.300
-That's the perfect way
to set it up.

00:12:05.300 --> 00:12:07.000
You did it exactly perfect.
[ Applause ]

00:12:07.000 --> 00:12:08.834
-Thank you.
-And wait till you see

00:12:08.834 --> 00:12:10.567
what happens and the twist.
It's really good.

00:12:10.567 --> 00:12:12.133
I want to show everyone a clip.
Here's Nick Kroll

00:12:12.133 --> 00:12:14.534
in "Don't Worry Darling."
Take a look.

